<title>USA: Shareholder sues Pacific Scientific, CEO.</title>
<headline>Shareholder sues Pacific Scientific, CEO.</headline>
<dateline>NEWPORT BEACH, Calif. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pacific Scientific Co said a shareholder sued it and its chief executive officer, Edgar Brower, alleging he made false and misleading statements about the company and its Solium subsidiary.</p>
<p>It said the suit, filed in the U.S. District Court in Central California, seeks damages and class action certification. It alleges that the false statements resulted in artifically inflating Pacific Scientific's share price Between October 1994 and July 1996.</p>
<p>Pacific Scientific denied the allegations and said it will vigorously defend itself.</p>
</text>
